TYPE=string
GROUP=lanes
DOC=THE DECLARED LANES — named scheduling partitions whose capacity does not compete with
DEFAULT<<'SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF'
    # THE DECLARED LANES — named scheduling partitions whose capacity does not compete with
    # SPIRA_MAX_DWARVES. A lane rune draws from its own RUNE_MAX_CONCURRENT rather than from
    # the pool, so the pool can be fully occupied by builders while the lane rune still has
    # room. This is what "ops cannot be starved by builders" has always meant; SPIRA_LANES
    # makes it declared configuration rather than a property implied by RUNE_ROLE=party.
    # A new lane is added here and given a name; runes join it with RUNE_LANE=<name>.
    # The ops and groomer lanes are declared by default because ops.rune and groomer.rune
    # ship using them. The qa lane is declared alongside them because qa.rune ships using it.
    # The mimir lane is declared because mimir.rune ships using it.
    # The czar lane is declared because czar.rune ships using it.
    # A lane rune still functions if its lane name is absent from this list (the mechanism is
    # RUNE_LANE set, not membership here), but the declaration makes it visible to operators
    # reading SPIRA_LANES for the list of scheduled partitions.
    # The warden lane is declared because warden.rune ships using it.
    # The mender lane is declared because mender.rune ships using it.
    # The pilgrimage lane is declared because pilgrim.rune ships using it.
    : "${SPIRA_LANES:=ops groomer qa mimir czar warden mender pilgrimage}"
SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF
